      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for to sprinkle (a powder), then the Hindi for to grind coarsely."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: गलाना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गलाना — galānā — \"to cook soft; to soften\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दाल को पूरी तरह गलाइए। Dāl ko pūrī tarah galāie. Cook the dal until it is completely soft."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने चावल गलाए, usne cāval galāe."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गलाना (galānā) is the causative of galnā, \"to melt, soften\", which CDIAL files under Sanskrit galati, \"drips, oozes, trickles\" (CDIAL 4074); CDIAL gives Hindi galnā as \"to melt, trickle\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
